    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:798680/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in health sciences",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher in health sciences Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral Researcher in health sciences Login and apply Faculty of Medicine, Health Sciences and Technology The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Doctoral Researcher to join the HealthEduCom Lab in the Research Unit of Health Sciences and Technology (HST), Faculty of Medicine, University of Oulu. The HealthEduCom Lab conducts multidisciplinary research on healthcare education, learning environments, mentoring and educator competence, predictive models of professional learning, and hybrid intelligence in extended reality (XR) contexts. The lab brings together expertise in health sciences, pedagogy, technology-enhanced learning and human-AI collaboration. You will work in an international research environment with access to the University of Oulu's Hybrid Intelligence research profile, the LEAF research infrastructure, and OuluHealth Labs in collaboration with the Wellbeing Services County of North Ostrobothnia. About the project The position is part of the Playful Entrepreneurial Minds: Playfulness and Hybrid Intelligence in Higher Education and Working Life (Playful Minds) project funded by the Research Council of Finland. The consortium brings together the University of Lapland, the University of Oulu and the University of Turku, together with national and international research and working-life partners. At the University of Oulu, we focus on hybrid intelligence, multirealities and playful learning in healthcare and medical education. Its overarching aim is to develop, implement, and validate a multidimensional Hybrid Intelligence-Playful Learning (HI-PL) framework that integrates playfulness, an entrepreneurial mindset, and hybrid intelligence into XR-based healthcare learning. The research uses a design-based research approach and combines qualitative, quantitative, behavioural and physiological data. About the job As a Doctoral Researcher, you will: Conduct doctoral research on hybrid intelligence-enabled playful learning in healthcare and medical education and complete a doctoral degree during the four-year employment period. Contribute to the co-design, implementation and validation of the HI-PL framework in nursing, health sciences and healthcare practice contexts. Plan and facilitate participatory workshops and pilot sessions with higher education students, academic professionals and healthcare professionals. Design and conduct controlled XR-based simulation studies involving playful human-AI interaction, metacognitive reflection, clinical decision-making and adaptive performance in demanding clinical scenarios. Collect and analyse multimodal research data, including questionnaires on playfulness, psychological safety, wellbeing, metacognition and engagement; behavioural and performance data from XR sessions and video recordings; and physiological indicators such as heart rate variability. Conduct interviews, focus groups and analyses of reflective learning logs to evaluate learning experiences, psychological safety, meaningful engagement and the usability of the HI-PL framework. Use design-based research and suitable qualitative, quantitative and mixed-method approaches to iteratively refine the framework and develop implementation guidance for healthcare curricula. Contribute to ethical review applications, research permissions, responsible data management, open science and GDPR-compliant research practices. Collaborate across the Playful Minds consortium and with national and international partners, including researchers in health sciences, education, learning sciences, technology and entrepreneurship. Complete doctoral studies at the University of Oulu Graduate School and publish the findings in high-quality international peer-reviewed journals and conferences. You will receive regular supervision and multidisciplinary support while gradually taking responsibility for your research questions, methodological choices, publications and international research profile. You will receive regular supervision and multidisciplinary support while gradually taking responsibility for your research questions, methodological choices, publications and international research profile. What we offer? A four-year, full-time Doctoral Researcher position in an ambitious multidisciplinary project addressing learning, wellbeing and professional competence in the era of hybrid intelligence. The support of the experienced and enthusiastic HealthEduCom Lab and the wider Playful Minds consortium, where you can share your expertise and grow as an independent researcher. Access to expertise in healthcare education, playful learning, hybrid intelligence, XR-based simulation, learning analytics, physiological measurement and mixed-method research. Access to relevant research infrastructure and authentic learning environments, including LEAF and OuluHealth Labs, subject to the final research protocols and permissions. Opportunities for national and international collaboration, conference participation, co-authored publications and research mobility when relevant to your doctoral project. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits. Development and career options of the big organization. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu . Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the position, we expect from you: A relevant Master's degree in health sciences / nursing science / health pedagogy. The degree must be completed before the employment begins . Eligibility to pursue doctoral studies and willingness to apply for doctoral study rights at the University of Oulu Graduate School at the beginning of the employment, unless you already hold the relevant study right. A strong motivation to conduct long-term doctoral research at the intersection of healthcare education, human-AI collaboration, playful learning and XR-based simulation. Foundational competence in research methods and readiness to develop expertise in qualitative, quantitative and mixed-method research. Ability to plan and carry out research responsibly, systematically and independently while working constructively in a multidisciplinary and international team. Good communication, collaboration and academic writing skills. Fluent written and spoken English. See also the requirements of the University of Oulu Graduate School (UniOGS) Experience in one or more of the following areas will be considered an advantage: Healthcare education, nursing or medical education, clinical practice, simulation-based education, or professional competence development. Hybrid intelligence, artificial intelligence in education, human-AI interaction, XR or other multireality learning environments. Design-based research, co-design, participatory research, intervention studies or experimental research. Qualitative methods such as interviews, focus groups, observations, content analysis or thematic analysis. Quantitative and mixed-method research, including questionnaire studies, multilevel modelling, structural equation modelling or correlation analysis. Collection or analysis of behavioural, video or physiological data, including heart rate variability. Relevant research software, for example R, SPSS, Stata, Mplus, NVivo or comparable tools. Research publications, conference presentations, open-science activities or previous work in a research project. Finnish language skills, especially for collaboration and data collection in Finnish healthcare and higher education contexts. Salary The position is fixed-term for four years as of 1.10.2026 or as soon as possible thereafter. The salary will be based on the levels 2-4 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 2500-3200 € per month (before taxes).  A trial period of 6 months is applied in the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 13.9.2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Cover letter CV following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity Research plan , maximum three pages plus references. Describe a feasible doctoral study aligned with the aims of a project. The final doctoral research plan will be refined together with the supervisors. List of publications , if applicable. Use a clear and standard academic format. The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, such as people of different ages, genders, and lingual, cultural, or minority groups. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Docent Heli Kuivila Research Unit of Health Sciences and Technology, Faculty of Medicine, University of Oulu Email: Heli-Maria.Kuivila@oulu.fi | Tel.: +358294485609 Professor Kristina Mikkonen Research Unit of Health Sciences and Technology, Faculty of Medicine, University of Oulu Email: kristina.mikkonen@oulu.fi | Tel.: +358 505754686 Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 % City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2025/138 Published 14.Aug.2026 Last application date 13.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:957102/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Geography, Faculty of Science",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Geography, Faculty of Science Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher, Geography, Faculty of Science Login and apply Faculty of Science, Geography The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Postdoctoral Researcher to work in a two (2) year fixed-term position with our talented freshwater plant research team for the project Unraveling the effects of contemporary and historical changes in climate and land use on freshwater biodiversity in high-latitude regions of Europe and North America . The project is the Kvantum Institute’s spearhead project for the period of 2025-2028. Description of the position We are looking for one (1) talented and highly motivated research-oriented person to carry out postdoctoral research addressing the effects of contemporary and historical changes in climate and land use on freshwater biodiversity in high-latitude regions of Europe and North America. The project aims to answer: Is land-use intensification a stronger driver of change than changing climate in explaining historical freshwater plant diversity and distribution? Are historical legacies of past climates and land use still shaping distribution and functions of present-day freshwater flora in Europe and North America? Are there long-lasting biotic imprints affecting contemporary freshwater plant communities, and do these legacies differ between continents? The postdoctoral researcher will conduct research in the project (in a fixed two (2) year term), publish research results in reputable international journals, and contribute to developing new proposals to further research in this area. Other duties may include teaching in undergraduate courses (up to 10% of the total 1612 working hours per year) and co-supervising master's and doctoral students. Also, you will present research in the Kvantum Institute’s Researchers’ Seminar and possibly international conferences. In addition, you may have to participate in administrative tasks of the university and/or the Geography Research Unit. Description of the research team The postdoctoral researcher will join a multinational research team of biogeographers and ecologists. Dr. Janne Alahuhta (University of Oulu, Finland), MSc Misha Tseitlin (University of Oulu), Dr. Jorge Garcia-Giron (University of Leon, Spain), Dr. Daniel Larkin (University of Minnesota, USA) and Dr. Danelle Larson (US Geological Survey, USA) make up the project’s core research team. The position will be based in the Physical Geography Research Group ( PGRG ) co-led by Senior Researcher Janne Alahuhta and located at the University of Oulu, Finland. PGRG contributes to cutting-edge global change research by focusing on a wide range of complementing study questions related to abiotic and biotic earth surface systems, including also Macrophyte Biogeography Lab led by Dr. Alahuhta. Qualification requirements for the Postdoctoral researcher position PhD in Geography, Ecology, Environmental Sciences, Biostatistics, or another related discipline. The doctoral degree must have been received no more than 10 years ago. Demonstrated experience in community ecology or species distribution modelling using R. Advanced level work in R (or Python) and previous experience in functional and phylogenetic biodiversity approaches are considered an additional asset. Knowledge of aquatic ecosystems and/or aquatic plant ecology is considered a benefit. Basic expertise in GIS (e.g. ArcGIS or QGIS) is required; advanced level in GIS is preferred. Experience managing and harmonizing heterogeneous ecological, environmental, climatic, or related datasets is required. Ability for independent scientific work. Open-minded and enthusiastic towards research. Fluency in both written and spoken English. Good communication and teamwork skills. Proven track record of securing competitive research funding (e.g., national research council, foundations) is considered a strong merit. When assessing the candidate’s merits for the position of Postdoctoral Researcher, attention will be paid to scientific excellence, such as research outputs, international scientific activities and collaboration, supervision of undergraduate students, pedagogical competence, societal relevance, impact and potential of scientific activities, and services for the academic community. What we offer You will become a part of a highly talented research group that is working on strategically and globally significant research areas. The support of an experienced and enthusiastic research team where you can share and grow your expertise. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits here. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. Development and career options of the big organization. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu . Salary The position is fixed-term for two (2) years as of 01.01.2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The project lasts until the end of 2028. The salary will be based on the levels 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 3900-4300 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 30.9.2026 (23:59 Finnish local time, UTC +3) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: A motivation letter (max. 2 pages) summarizing the applicant’s professional experience and expertise and describing why the applicant is interested in this position. Also, information on personal research interests, experience, and career plans are highly encouraged. CV , following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of publications , following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland Contact information of two senior/experienced researchers who may be asked to give a statement on the candidate The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Senior Researcher Janne Alahuhta, Geography Research Unit, janne.alahuhta@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Employment expires 2028-12-31 Contract type Full time First day of employment 1.1.2027 Salary TES Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/490 Contact Janne Alahuhta, 050-3662601, janne.alahuhta@oulu.fi Published 14.Aug.2026 Last application date 30.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:958304/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, in the FRONT research programme",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, in the FRONT research programme Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher, in the FRONT research programme Login and apply Faculty of Education and Psychology, Teacher education, school and society The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Postdoctoral Researcher to join us in the Frontiers of Arctic and Global Resilience (FRONT) research programme at the University of Oulu. The postdoctoral researcher position will be placed in the Faculty of Education and Psychology. The FRONT research programme forms a part of our national profiling actions supported by the Research Council of Finland. FRONT programme focuses on changing human-environment relations and challenges to cope and adapt with that change and aims to ground-breaking transdisciplinary research on resilience and how to ‘Adapt for Our Future’ in the Arctic and elsewhere on the planet. The programme involves cutting-edge research to advance the existing frontiers of knowledge on systemic changes needed for resilience planning and governance, and for finding solutions to the wicked problems of resilience across the social and environmental sciences. FRONT focuses on international top-level collaborative and transdisciplinary research on socio-economic and socio-ecological resilience in different scales across social and environmental sciences, supported by the new Resilience Academy. By bringing together international, national and University of Oulu-based scholars from across disciplines, and encouraging effective public communication of science, FRONT will promote inter- and transdisciplinary and citizen-engaged studies of the environment and raise the University’s profile as an international leader in addressing the challenges of humans in change and human impacts and dependency on environment. About the job We are looking for a postdoctoral researcher in psychology (social psychology, environmental psychology, political psychology, developmental psychology etc.), education, or a neighboring social science field. The two-year project will be exploring “critical emotional awareness (CEA)” (Ojala, 2023, 2026) as a possible resilience factor against disinformation/propaganda and for civic engagement among young people in a time of polycrisis (climate change, war etc.). The age groups in focus in the project are young people between late childhood and up to young adulthood. The preliminary plan is that the post doc in collaboration with the project leader will: (1) Conduct interviews to explore young people’s emotions, and views about emotions, in relation to different intertwined societal problems (polycrisis), analyze, write, and publish an article on the data. (2) Based on earlier research and the interviews and in collaboration with young people create a survey scale capturing CEA, test how this scale works in groups of young people and publish articles on the data. Besides working in FRONT, you will work together with colleagues in the SERSus (Socio-Ecological Resilience and Sustainability) research group, led by Prof. Maria Ojala (who is also the project leader of this post doc project), at the Faculty of Education and Psychology, University of Oulu. As a postdoctoral researcher you will also Collaborate in service to FRONT programme, faculty, and university Participate in the development and activities of the Resilience Academy of Oulu (RAO) Engage in writing and submitting applications for research funding Take part in teaching activities, subject to faculty and research unit needs and your own teaching/research capabilities and interests What we offer We offer you a supportive academic environment in a community of committed scholars and the possibility to make use of funding opportunities to generate new research ideas and build an innovative programme that will attract international scholars. The University of Oulu offers flexible working hours, an excellent work-life balance and provides a range of occupational healthcare services. Our competitive salaries include paid leave and an additional holiday bonus in the summer. The support of an experienced and enthusiastic team of people, with whom you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits here. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. Development and career options of the big organization. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu . What we expect A doctoral degree in a relevant field that was awarded not more than ten years ago Skills in advanced statistical analyses and a solid experience in working with quantitative survey studies and preferably with scale development Experience of qualitative methods in the form of conducting interviews and analyzing interview data Good, demonstrated capacity to collaborate in research and research dissemination activities Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills in English We also appreciate: Knowledge of other methodological approaches and multidisciplinary experience A transdisciplinary research orientation with demonstrated research experience or interest Earlier experience of research about emotions in a societal context Earlier experience of psychological or educational research about climate change and other sustainability issues As a person you are creative, analytical, curious, open to other scientific disciplines, and can conduct excellent research in a novel subfield. When assessing the candidate’s merits for the position of Postdoctoral Researcher, attention will also be paid to scientific excellence, such as research outputs, international scientific activities and collaboration, supervision of undergraduate students, pedagogical competence, societal relevance, impact and potential of scientific activities, and services for the academic community. Salary The position is fixed-term for two years, starting at the latest on 1st of January 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The salary will be based on the levels 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 3700-4300 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 30th of September 2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Cover letter CV , following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of publications , following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland Certificates/Diplomas: Scanned copy of the original Ph.D. degree certificate and, when necessary, official translations to Finnish or English. In case the degree is still in process, please give an official notification from the supervisor or faculty to address the estimated date of defense. Contact information of two senior/experienced researchers who may be asked to give a statement on the candidate. The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact FRONT coordinator Dr Lotta Haukipuro (lotta.haukipuro@oulu.fi) or the project leader Prof. Maria Ojala (maria.ojala@oulu.fi) Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/501 Contact Lotta Haukipuro, lotta.haukipuro@oulu.fi Maria Ojala, maria.ojala@oulu.fi Published 14.Aug.2026 Last application date 30.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:948111/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher, Multimodal AI and Physiological Sensing for Cardiometabolic Health",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher, Multimodal AI and Physiological Sensing for Cardiometabolic Health Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral Researcher, Multimodal AI and Physiological Sensing for Cardiometabolic Health Login and apply Faculty of Medicine, Health Sciences and Technology The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Doctoral Researcher to join a multidisciplinary research environment spanning two faculties at the University of Oulu: the Research Unit of Health Sciences and Technology (HST), Faculty of Medicine the Center for Machine Vision and Signal Analysis (CMVS), Computer Science and Engineering, Faculty of Information Technology and Electrical Engineering The position offers a distinctive opportunity to conduct research at the intersection of artificial intelligence, signal processing, computer vision, and digital health. The objective of the position is to carry out high-quality doctoral research and to complete a doctoral degree during the four-year employment period. About the job The position is part of the Research Council of Finland-funded Academy Research Fellow project led by Dr. Xiaoting Wu: CARDIAB: Towards Cardiometabolic Intelligence—Decoding Heart Dynamics for AI-Augmented Diabetes Monitoring and Human Sustainable Wellbeing . As a doctoral researcher, you will: Conduct doctoral research on multimodal physiological sensing and AI-based analysis of cardiac dynamics. Process and analyze ECG, PPG, camera-based physiological measurements, and radar signals. Contribute to the design of data collection protocols, sensor synchronization, data annotation, and research data management. Evaluate associations between multimodal physiological patterns, diabetes-related factors, and broader indicators of cardiometabolic health. Collaborate with researchers from computer science, engineering, health sciences, and medicine. Complete doctoral studies at the University of Oulu Graduate School. Publish research findings in high-quality international journals and conferences. What we offer A fully funded, full-time doctoral researcher position for four years. Joint multidisciplinary research support from the Faculty of Medicine and the Faculty of Information Technology and Electrical Engineering. Access to expertise in artificial intelligence, computer vision, physiological signal analysis, biomedical engineering, digital health, and health sciences. Access to multimodal sensing equipment, experimental facilities, research datasets, and computational resources. Opportunities for international collaboration, conference participation, and research visits when relevant to the doctoral project. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits. Development and career options of the big organization. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the position, we require from you: Master's degree in a relevant field, such as computer science, electronic engineering, data science, or a comparable discipline. A Master's degree must have been completed before the start of the doctoral researcher's work. Strong programming and data processing skills with C/C++/Matlab/python. Foundational knowledge of machine learning, digital signal processing, and statistical data analysis. Motivation to conduct long-term doctoral research in a multidisciplinary environment. Fluent in written and spoken English. The ability to work both independently and collaboratively. You must apply for the right to study for a doctoral degree at the beginning of your employment in accordance with the requirements of the University of Oulu Graduate School (UniOGS). We also appreciate experience in physiological or biomedical signal processing. computer vision or camera-based physiological measurements. research publications, open-source software, or previous research projects. Salary The position is full-time and a fixed term for 4 years. The employment will begin as soon as possible after the completion of the recruitment process. The salary will be based on levels 2-4 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50% of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 2500-3200 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 5.9.2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Cover letter, maximum one page. Introduce yourself and explain your motivation for applying, your interest in the research topic, and how your academic background supports the proposed doctoral research. CV following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity. Research plan, maximum three pages+ references , following the guidelines of the Academy of Finland. The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas and transcripts, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Dr. Xiaoting Wu University of Oulu Email: xiaoting.wu@oulu.fi Prof. Kristina Mikkonen University of Oulu Email: kristina.mikkonen@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/452 Published 13.Aug.2026 Last application date 05.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:957902/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher, In-situ and Operando Spectroscopy and Scattering Techniques for Oxygen Evolution Reaction Mechanism Studies, Faculty of Science",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher, In-situ and Operando Spectroscopy and Scattering Techniques for Oxygen Evolution Reaction Mechanism Studies, Faculty of Science Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral Researcher, In-situ and Operando Spectroscopy and Scattering Techniques for Oxygen Evolution Reaction Mechanism Studies, Faculty of Science Login and apply Faculty of Science, Nano and Molecular Systems The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Doctoral Researcher in In-situ and Operando Spectroscopy and Scattering Techniques for Oxygen Evolution Reaction Mechanism Studies to join us in the Nano and Molecular Systems Research Unit at the Faculty of Science. About the job The doctoral researcher will join an interdisciplinary research project focused on understanding the reaction mechanisms of the oxygen evolution reaction (OER) using advanced in-situ and operando spectroscopy and scattering techniques. The project combines electrochemistry, materials science, spectroscopy, synchrotron radiation, and computational data analysis to reveal the structural, electronic, and chemical evolution of electrocatalysts under realistic operating conditions. The research will involve the design and development of advanced electrochemical cells compatible with laboratory- and synchrotron-based characterization techniques. The successful candidate will work closely with collaborators and participate in experimental studies at leading synchrotron radiation facilities. As a Doctoral Researcher, you will: Design, develop, and optimize in-situ and operando electrochemical cells for spectroscopy and scattering experiments. Assemble, commission, and maintain experimental setups for advanced electrochemical and spectroscopic measurements. Carry out in-situ and operando Raman spectroscopy to monitor catalyst phase evolution, surface intermediates, and reaction pathways during oxygen evolution. Perform in-situ/operando synchrotron-based experimental studies employing advanced operando characterization techniques, including X-ray absorption spectroscopy (XAS), X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS), high-energy X-ray diffraction (HEXRD), total scattering, and other complementary spectroscopy and scattering methods. Process, analyze, and interpret multimodal datasets obtained from Raman spectroscopy, XRD, XPS, XAS, and electrochemical experiments to establish structure–property–performance relationships. Develop computational workflows and automated data-processing pipelines using Python, MATLAB, and other scientific software for handling large laboratory and synchrotron datasets. Perform quantitative spectral fitting, kinetic analysis, multivariate statistical analysis, visualization, and data integration to correlate catalyst structure, oxidation state, and reaction kinetics under operating conditions. Present research findings at national/international conferences and publish results in leading peer-reviewed scientific journals. Contribute to the supervision of Bachelor's and Master's students and participate in teaching activities within the research unit. What we offer The successful candidate will receive comprehensive training in advanced operando spectroscopy and scattering techniques, electrochemistry, synchrotron radiation experiments, scientific programming, and multimodal data analysis. The project provides access to state-of-the-art laboratory instrumentation and leading international synchrotron facilities, offering opportunities to collaborate with internationally recognized researchers and contribute to cutting-edge research in sustainable energy materials. The doctoral researcher will develop expertise spanning experimental design, advanced characterization, computational data analysis, and mechanistic understanding of electrocatalytic reactions, providing an excellent foundation for a future career in academia, national laboratories, or industry. In addition, we offer: Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits. Development and career options of the big organization. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Who are you? We expect you to have: An MSc degree in Physics, Materials Science, Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Strong interest in electrocatalysis, renewable energy technologies, and advanced materials characterization. Experience with one or more experimental techniques such as Raman spectroscopy, X-ray diffraction (XRD), X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS), X-ray absorption spectroscopy (XAS), electron microscopy, or electrochemical characterization is a plus. Experience with scientific programming and data analysis using Python, MATLAB, or similar programming languages. Knowledge of spectral processing, curve fitting, statistical analysis, scientific visualization, and handling large experimental datasets is considered plus. Excellent written and spoken English. Strong analytical thinking, problem-solving ability, and the capability to work both independently and as part of an international multidisciplinary research team. Willingness to travel and participate in experimental campaigns at synchrotron radiation facilities. You must apply for the right to study for a doctoral degree at the beginning of your employment in accordance with the requirements of the University of Oulu Graduate School (UniOGS). Salary The position is fixed-term for 4 years as of 1.10.2026 or as soon as possible thereafter. The salary will be based on the levels 2-4 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 2600-3200 € per month (before taxes).  A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 11.9.2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Cover letter CV following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity Narrative CV , using the given template (more information: principles for the assessment of research and researchers at the University of Oulu ) The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Dr. Ekta Rani, Faculty of Science, Nano and Molecular Systems Research Unit, ekta.rani@oulu.fi Dr. Samuli Urpelainen, Faculty of Science, Nano and Molecular Systems Research Unit, samuli.urpelainen@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/495 Published 12.Aug.2026 Last application date 11.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/what:subscribe/": {
      "title": "Työpaikkavahti",
      "description": "Paikkavahti Kirjaudu Varbi-tilillesi Ruotsi Englanti Norja Tanska Saksa Alankomaat Kiina (BETA) Puola Ranska Romania Uusnorja Työpaikkavahti Haluatko ilmoituksen uusista työpaikoista? Aseta työpaikkavahti ja saa päivittäisiä tai viikoittaisia päivityksiä valintoihisi sopivista työpaikoista. Vahti on voimassa kaksi vuotta, mutta voit peruuttaa luodun vahdin milloin tahansa. (Voit luoda useita vahteja.) Kuinka usein haluat sähköpostia? Joka päivä Joka viikko Sähköposti * Hyväksyn, että Grade Varbi AB tallentaa yllä olevat tiedot ja jakaa sähköpostitse tietoja avoimista työpaikoista. Voin peruuttaa tilauksen minkä tahansa työpaikkailmoituksen sähköpostiviestissä olevan linkin kautta. Työpaikkavahti - RSS Työpaikkavahti RSS-syötteenä https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/what:rssfeed/ Poista työpaikkavahti Kirjoita sähköpostiosoitteesi tähän Poista Takaisin avoimiin työpaikkoihin Grade Varbi Recruit rekrytointijärjestelmä Evästeet Ehdot Tietosuojakäytäntö Saavutettavuusseloste × Modal title Käytämme evästeitä sisäänkirjautumiseen, käyttökokemuksen parantamiseen, jakolinkkien tarjoamiseen sekä joissakin tapauksissa markkinointiin ja tilastojen keräämiseen. Hyväksy kaikki evästeet Hyväksy vain tarpeelliset Lue lisää evästeistä tässä ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:946853/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, History, Culture and Communication Studies",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, History, Culture and Communication Studies Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher, History, Culture and Communication Studies Login and apply Humanistinen tiedekunta, Historia, kulttuuri ja viestintätieteet The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Researcher in Propaganda Studies to join the History, Culture and Communications Unit in the Faculty of Humanities at the University of Oulu. The successful candidate will develop and implement an independent research plan focusing on propaganda, understood as the deliberate dissemination of biased, selective, or misleading information intended to shape public opinion in support of, or opposition to, a particular cause, individual, group, institution, or movement.  Applicants are encouraged to propose their own conceptual, theoretical, and methodological approaches to the study of propaganda. Research may examine political, social, cultural, technological, or informational dimensions of propaganda and may employ qualitative, quantitative, computational, historical, or mixed methods designs. The proposed research should be grounded in the social sciences and/or humanities and should address contemporary or recent (21st-century) forms of propaganda, focusing on Northern European societies. The position is part of the SafeEarth research programme which integrates the University of Oulu’s specialised research areas in space security, cybersecurity, and human security. Within SafeEarth, the position is connected to the themes “Language use, information practices and security” and “Information warfare and cybersecurity”. The researchers will work in collaboration with Professor Kari Alenius (History) and Professor Noora Hirvonen (Information Studies), and their respective research teams. Professor Alenius and his team focus on political propaganda, including strategic communication and information warfare conducted by state actors, parties, and ideological groups. Their research examines the objectives of propaganda and the reasons why particular methods are employed, with a particular emphasis on the present and recent history. Professor Hirvonen and her team build on sociocultural and sociotechnical information practice research and examine how contemporary propaganda is encountered, experienced, and interacted with in everyday life, particularly among young people. Their research aims to advance understanding of both the first-hand experiences of propaganda and of the situational and globally interconnected information environments and structures that shape the emergence of such experiences. Beyond advancing understanding of propaganda, both research groups are motivated by the need to support the development of strategies to countering harmful information influence, particularly through strengthening media and information literacy. In today’s media and information environments, where information influence efforts have become increasingly complex, multimodal, and difficult to detect, research on propaganda offers important tools for understanding how information is used to shape perceptions, attitudes, and public opinion. By generating knowledge that can inform public debate, decision making, education, and media practices, such research has the potential to contribute to countering harmful influence activities, reducing polarization, fostering critical thinking, and strengthening societal security and resilience. We expect the recruited researcher to align their planned activities with these broader objectives. About the job As a Postdoctoral Researcher your primary duties will include: Planning and conducting independent research on propaganda, from a selected viewpoint. Producing academic contributions in the form of articles and/or monographs. Actively participating and facilitating interdisciplinary work between the different subjects of the History, Culture, and Communication Studies Research Unit and within the SafeEarth programme. Participating in outreach initiatives that engage both academic and non-academic publics. Engaging in writing and submitting applications for further research funding. Contributing to teaching (max. 5% of your total working time). Other administrative and community activities linked to academic life at the University of Oulu. What we offer The support of two subjects (History, Information Studies), with whom you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Development and career options of a big organization. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits here. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu . Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the Postdoctoral Researcher position, we require from you: Doctoral degree in a relevant field (history, information studies, communication studies, or equivalent). The doctoral degree must have been completed by the closing date for applications. The doctoral degree must be received no more than 10 years ago. Experience in relevant social scientiﬁc or humanities research evidenced by peer-reviewed publications. An interest in issues relevant to propaganda in the Northern European cultural sphere. Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills in English. Proven teamwork skills and commitment to academic collaboration. Ability to engage in independent scientific research Teaching competence required for the position We also appreciate An interdisciplinary and/or transdisciplinary research orientation. Existing research and/or practitioner experience of issues related to propaganda. Conversational level of Finnish. When assessing the candidate’s merits, attention will be paid to scientific excellence, such as research outputs, international scientific activities and collaboration, supervision of undergraduate students, pedagogical competence, societal relevance, impact and potential of scientific activities, and services for the academic community. Salary The position is fixed term for 3 years as of 1st January 2027. The salary will be based on the levels 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50% of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 3700-4300 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 1st October 2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in Finnish or English and include the following: Letter of motivation (max. 1 page) summarizing your professional experience and expertise and describing why you are interested in the position CV (max. 4 pages), following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of publications , following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland , with up to five key publications relevant to the position marked in bold Research concept paper (max. 2-3 pages; references do not count towards this limit) for a potential project in the topic of the position. The plan should include information about any potential empirical work linked to it and a section that discusses its engagement with the thematic areas mentioned above Contact information of two to three senior/experienced researchers who may be asked to give a personal statement about you (note that these will only be requested if you are shortlisted for this position) The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Professor Kari Alenius (kari.alenius@oulu.fi) or Professor Noora Hirvonen (noora.hirvonen@oulu.fi) Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time First day of employment 1 January 2027 Salary TES Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/432 Contact Kari Petteri Alenius, kari.alenius@oulu.fi Noora Hirvonen, 0000000000, noora.hirvonen@oulu.fi Published 11.Sep.2026 Last application date 01.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:967309/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Mathematical Sciences, Faculty of Science",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Mathematical Sciences, Faculty of Science Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher, Mathematical Sciences, Faculty of Science Login and apply Faculty of Science, Mathematical Sciences The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Postdoctoral Researcher to join us in the Research Group on Computational Uncertainty Quantification at the Faculty of Science, University of Oulu. The Research Group on Computational Uncertainty Quantification develops mathematical and computational methods for quantifying uncertainty in inverse problems. Our research combines rigorous mathematical analysis, Bayesian methods, and scalable computational approaches, with applications ranging from imaging and sensing to industrial inverse problems. The group is part of the Mathematical Sciences Research Unit and works closely with the Inverse Problems research community at the University of Oulu, as well as national and international collaborators. About the job The position focuses on developing new mathematical and computational methods for Bayesian inverse problems and uncertainty quantification. A particular emphasis will be placed on the design and analysis of new Bayesian prior models for inverse problems and on developing methods for exploring complex high-dimensional and potentially infinite-dimensional posterior distributions. As a postdoctoral researcher, you will: conduct independent and collaborative research in applied mathematics, with a particular focus on Bayesian inverse problems and computational uncertainty quantification. develop and analyse new classes of Bayesian priors for inverse problems, including their mathematical properties and computational implementation. develop new mathematical and computational methods for exploring high-dimensional and potentially infinite-dimensional posterior distributions. contribute to the development and implementation of research software, particularly in Python, for computational uncertainty quantification and inverse problems. conduct research in connection with the SPARSe Academy Research Fellowship project and the Finnish Centre of Excellence in Randomness and Structures (FAME) Flagship , and contribute to ongoing international collaborations, including collaboration with researchers at Johannes Kepler University Linz and industrial partners. These collaborations aim, among other objectives, to develop mathematical and computational uncertainty quantification methods that can be made accessible and useful for industrial applications. contribute to the supervision of undergraduate and graduate students and participate in the research activities of the group. contribute to teaching in mathematics and applied mathematics according to the needs of the research unit. be part of the Research Group on Computational Uncertainty Quantification , led by Assistant Professor Babak Maboudi Afkham, and interact closely with the broader inverse problems research community at the University of Oulu. be part of the FAME Flagship on a broader scale and have opportunities to interact with its national and international network of researchers and collaborators. What we offer The support of an experienced and enthusiastic research team, with whom you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits here. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. Development and career options of the big organization. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu . Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the position, we require from you: Doctoral degree in mathematics, applied mathematics, or a closely related field , with a strong mathematical background, particularly in analysis. The doctoral degree must have been completed by the closing date for applications. The degree must have been obtained no more than 10 years ago. Ability to engage in independent scientific research. Teaching skills required for the position. Strong background in mathematical analysis and the mathematical foundations relevant to inverse problems and uncertainty quantification. Strong software development and scientific computing skills, particularly in Python. Ability and motivation to conduct both theoretical and computational research. Fluent written and spoken English. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of an interdisciplinary and international research environment. We also appreciate: A strong background in pseudodifferential operator theory . Previous research experience in inverse problems, Bayesian inverse problems, uncertainty quantification, or closely related areas. Experience with high-dimensional or infinite-dimensional Bayesian inference. Experience in developing computational methods for inverse problems or statistical inference. Experience in supervising students or contributing to university-level teaching. Experience with collaborative research involving researchers from different disciplines or industrial partners. Finnish language skills. When assessing the candidate’s merits for the position of Postdoctoral Researcher, attention will be paid to scientific excellence, such as research outputs, international scientific activities and collaboration, supervision of undergraduate students, pedagogical competence, societal relevance, impact and potential of scientific activities, and services for the academic community. Salary The position is fixed-term for three years, starting on November 1 or as soon as possible thereafter. The salary will be based on the levels 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 3700-4300 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 22.9.2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Cover letter CV , following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity Narrative CV , using the provided template ( principles for the assessment of research and researchers at the University of Oulu ) List of publications , following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland Teaching Portfolio , following the guidelines of the University of Oulu The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Assistant Professor Babak Maboudi Afkham, Faculty of Science, Mathematical Sciences Research Unit, University of Oulu, babak.maboudi@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time First day of employment 1.11.2026 Salary TES Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/564 Published 09.Sep.2026 Last application date 22.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:909322/": {
      "title": "Project worker, IKAPO project",
      "description": "Project worker, IKAPO project Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Project worker, IKAPO project Login and apply Faculty of Information Technology and Electrical Engineering The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are looking for an enthusiastic and efficient Project Worker For the Development Team, Faculty of Information Technology and Electrical Engineering (ITEE), University of Oulu for the period of 27 October 2026 – 31 December 2027 with a 40% work contract. Are you the enthusiastic and efficient Project Worker we are looking for to help us with turning data, participation, and partnerships into real opportunities and impact for students and companies? As a project worker, you will join ITEE’s IKAPO project, which aims to optimise ICT expert resources and strengthens innovation capacity in micro, small, and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs). IKAPO’s new partnership programme and model for recruitment, work-life encounters, and alumni cooperation foster interaction and channel students’ skills to create value and opportunities for both students and MSMEs. Co-funded by the European Union, the project boosts international students’ career paths, professional development, and smoother employment in North Ostrobothnia. We are looking for… A Project Worker for ITEE’s Development Team. As a project worker, you will: Develop websites, company collaboration platforms, AI-powered analytics solutions, and digital tools supporting the goals of the IKAPO project, including the ITEE SPOT collaboration platform. Participate in identifying company needs and promoting student projects (e.g. within the ArkiDigi initiative www.ikapo.fi/arkidigi-brochure ), traineeships, thesis assignments, and other forms of university-industry collaboration within IKAPO project. Compile and deliver company-specific analytics and insights that support collaboration opportunities, skills matching, responding to companies’ recruitment needs, and project impact assessment. Support interaction between students and companies through events and programme activities that strengthen student engagement, employability, and university-industry collaboration. Produce and share impactful content and means of engagement (e.g. event infos, slide decks, web articles, social media posts) Work closely with student communities, staff, and external partners of the project/faculty. What we expect from you Ongoing, well-progressing studies in one of the degree programmes of the Faculty of Information Technology and Electrical Engineering (ITEE) at the University of Oulu. Strong analytical, development, and IT skills, along with the ability to utilise AI tools for compiling, managing, and analyzing large datasets; knowledge on efficient use of AI agents; ability to administer and evolve e.g. Wix/SharePoint sites and other web-based tools (iteespot.ikapo.fi & course-matcher-pro.ikapo.fi). Positive, proactive mindset, self‑direction, and solid problem‑solving skills; strong teamwork skills in an international working environment. Fluent communication and confident presenting in English; ability to produce clear, high‑quality content in English and draft working translations into Finnish when needed. Previous experience in planning and delivering programmes and or events. Strong organisational skills and a systematic, goal-oriented approach, with proven ability to manage time effectively and prioritise tasks to achieve impactful outcomes. Experience with survey tools (e.g., Webropol, Microsoft Forms) and with visualising & reporting findings (graphs, infographics, presentations). Proficiency in PowerPoint and image/publishing tools (e.g., Canva, Photoshop, InDesign). Understanding of student wellbeing and a motivation to facilitate students’ smooth transition to working life; familiarity with student communities and communication channels to ensure engagement and impact. We also appreciate Knowledge of Finland’s industry landscape and ITEE’s core technology domains Interest in supporting micro and SME companies through well‑scoped student project, traineeship and thesis placements that create mutual value. Video creation/editing skills. Developing Finnish language skills. Driving licence and a possibility to use a car. What we offer? The support of an experienced and enthusiastic team, where you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being, and flexible multi-location and remote work opportunities. Read more about other staff benefits. Development and career options of the big organisation. Work that matters! Read more about working with us. Salary The position is part time (40 %) and fixed term from 27 October 2026 to 31 December 2027. The salary will be based on the levels 3 of the demand level chart for other expert and support staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50% of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary in comparable part-time positions is typically 1000-1100 € permonth (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply Complete your application by 29 September 2026 23:59 (Finnish local time). Please attach your CV, a concise motivation letter in English, transcript of records, and 2–5 references (or a short portfolio) showcasing relevant analytics/AI, survey/reporting, event/programme organisation, and/or content creation work. In the references, please describe briefly the outcome and your role in the implementation. We will invite candidates for live interviews to be held on 1 October. Contact information If you have any further questions, please contact Development manager Hanna Saarela, hanna.saarela@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 40% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/198 Published 16.Sep.2026 Last application date 29.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:964405/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in snow and microclimate processes of cold-climate ecosystems",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher in snow and microclimate processes of cold-climate ecosystems Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher in snow and microclimate processes of cold-climate ecosystems Login and apply Faculty of Technology, Water, Energy and Environmental Engineering The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Postdoctoral Researcher in snow and microclimate processes of cold-climate ecosystems for a 3-year fixed-term position to join us in the Faculty of Technology, Water, Energy and Environmental Engineering Unit. About the job We are seeking a postdoctoral researcher to join our team to study changes and patterns in hydrology, snow and microclimates across Arctic, boreal and alpine ecosystems, and to connect their dynamics to ecological processes in cold climates. We welcome applicants with backgrounds in hydrology, remote sensing, data science, physical geography, environmental science, ecosystem science or ecology, as long as you bring strong numerical and programming skills and a genuine interest in cold-climate systems. We recognise that excellent candidates come from different scientific traditions. We therefore invite applications along two complementary profiles, and encourage you to indicate in your application which profile best matches your interests and expertise. Both profiles are equally valued and will be assessed on their own merits. We also welcome candidates whose expertise and interests fall between these profiles or combine elements of both. Profile A — Snow, climate and remote sensing (technical / modelling focus). You will study snow-related processes and the impacts of climate change on them in Arctic, boreal and alpine ecosystems by combining remote sensing tools, microclimate datasets and mechanistic models. You will utilise and develop advanced mechanistic and deep-learning models with fine-resolution satellite imagery and empirical microclimate data to understand and predict the localised effects of climate change and human impacts on cold-climate hydrology and snow. This profile suits a hydrological modeller or data scientist with a strong background in spatial datasets and analyses and deep understanding in cold-climate processes. Profile B — Snow, microclimate and ecosystems (interdisciplinary focus). You will study the dynamics and spatial patterns in snow and hydrological and microclimate conditions and link them to ecological processes in Arctic, boreal and alpine ecosystems. You will investigate how shifts in snow cover, local hydrology and microclimates propagate through cold ecosystems affecting vegetation, biodiversity and ecosystem functions. This profile suits a hydrologist, physical geographer, ecosystem scientist or ecologist with strong numerical and programming skills and an understanding of cold-ecosystem processes and nature. The position is linked to a project led by Assistant Professor Pekka Niittynen that studies local-scale trends in snow cover duration and their ecological implications across Arctic and alpine ecosystems. The postdoctoral position is also linked to large-scale and long-term research in the water sector at the Flagship DIWA - Digital Waters , and SAFIRE - Safeguarding Biodiversity through Interdisciplinary Research on Habitat Restoration- a Profi8 programme at the University of Oulu, funded by the Research Council Finland. SAFIRE’s focus is the production of scientifically excellent and actionable knowledge on habitat restoration, especially in Arctic regions. The position is located at the Water, Energy and Environmental Engineering research unit, in the Faculty of Technology. Our water research team includes 5 research groups with a strong focus on various aspects of water engineering, including hydrological modelling, cold climate hydrology, hydrological process studies, and groundwater research. In hydrology, the research includes studies at our research stations and supersites in Finland with a unique and developing infrastructure. The position is also linked to the Arctic, Antarctic and Mountain initiative , a network of ~150 researchers across the world that works on global microclimate datasets and promotes microclimate research across disciplines. Your responsibilities The responsibilities below are tailored to your chosen profile, with shared responsibilities common to both. Shared responsibilities: Integrate remote sensing observations, climate reanalysis and microclimate data to reconstruct historical snow, hydrological and microclimate trends. Collaborate with ecologists, hydrologists and modellers to assess the impacts of hydrological and cryospheric changes on ecosystems and water resources. Publish high-quality research and contribute to open-source tools. Depending on personal interest, field work in northern Finland, Sweden and Norway is possible. Participate in doctoral supervision and education. In addition, for Profile A: Develop algorithms for fine-scale snow and hydrological mapping and modelling utilising Landsat, Sentinel and PlanetScope satellite data. Advance mechanistic, deep-learning or hybrid models that translate satellite and microclimate data into predictions of snow and hydrological change. In addition, for Profile B: Analyse how changes in snow, hydrology and microclimate propagate to ecological processes in Arctic and alpine tundra and boreal forests. Bridge physical environmental data and model outputs with ecological and biodiversity datasets and outcomes. What we offer We offer you an interesting and versatile position as part of a large and growing digital water research cluster in Finland and the SAFIRE profiling research team. We help you to grow and realise your full scientific potential and contribution. You will have the opportunity to develop professionally with the help of an experienced and enthusiastic team. You will also have access to our unique global infrastructure, where innovative studies can be initiated in collaboration with our team members. The University of Oulu offers Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits. Development and career options of the big organization. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Who are you? To succeed in the position, you are required to have: A relevant doctoral degree in hydrology, remote sensing, data science, environmental science, ecosystem science, ecology, physical geography or a related field. The doctoral degree must have been completed by the closing date for applications. The degree must have been obtained no more than 10 years ago. Ability to engage in independent scientific research. Teaching skills required for the position. Strong background in numerical modelling and data analysis. Experience with programming languages such as R, Python, Julia, Fortran or C/C++. Excellent written and spoken English. Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team. Strong experience in scientific writing and excellent communication skills. We also appreciate the following: Experience with satellite remote sensing data and analyses. Experience with collecting and analysing drone imagery. Understanding of cold-ecosystem processes and nature, and experience linking environmental drivers to ecological or biodiversity outcomes. Experience with ecological, hydrological or microclimate field measurements in cold regions. Familiarity with high-performance computing and environments. Experience in supervision or co-supervision of doctoral researchers. International experience and networking skills. Experience in proposal writing. When assessing the candidate's merits for the position of Postdoctoral Researcher, attention will be paid to scientific excellence, such as research outputs, international scientific activities and collaboration, supervision of undergraduate students, pedagogical competence, societal relevance, impact and potential of scientific activities, and services for the academic community, as well as prior experience in working with cold-climate topics. Salary The position is a fixed-term position for 3 years, beginning on 1.12.2026 (or as soon as possible thereafter). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. The salary will be based on the level 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities, depending on your qualifications. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). Typical monthly salary for a post-doctoral researcher is 3700 - 4800 € (before taxes), depending on your experience and qualifications. How to apply? Apply online at the latest by October 15, 2026 (23:59 Finnish time). The application should be written in English and include the following documents: A letter of motivation containing a short description of the research you propose to conduct in the position (max 2 pages) An academic Curriculum Vitae (max 4 pages) following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of 10 most important publications : select maximum of 10 scientific articles that highlight your research interests and competence and explain your role in them. Teaching and supervision experience (2 pages) Eligible applicants best fitting the expected research profile may be invited to an on-site or remote interview. All applicants will be notified when the selection process is completed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Further information Assistant Professor Pekka Niittynen, pekka.niittynen@oulu.fi Associate Professor Hannu Marttila, hannu.marttila@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/551 Published 16.Sep.2026 Last application date 15.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:964690/": {
      "title": "Lehtori, luokanopettaja, Oulun Normaalikoulu",
      "description": "Lehtori, luokanopettaja, Oulun Normaalikoulu Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Lehtori, luokanopettaja, Oulun Normaalikoulu Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Kasvatustieteiden ja psykologian tiedekunta, Oulun yliopiston harjoittelukoulu Oulun yliopisto on monitieteinen, kansainvälisesti toimiva tiedeyliopisto, jonka noin 4000 työntekijää tuottavat korkeatasoiseen tutkimukseen pohjautuvaa uutta tietoa ja antavat tutkimukseen perustuvaa opetusta kestävämmän, älykkäämmän ja inhimillisemmän maailman rakentamiseksi. Oulun yliopistoyhteisössä toimii kaikkiaan noin 19 000 henkilöä. Pohjoisen tiedeyhteisömme toiminta on globaalisti vaikuttavaa ja luo edellytyksiä innovaatioiden syntymiselle. Kaikkea tutkimus-, opetus- ja työyhteisötoimintaamme ohjaavat yliopistomme arvot sekä eettiset periaatteet. Oulun normaalikoulu on Oulun yliopiston harjoittelukoulu. Koulussamme opiskelee noin 900 oppilasta perusasteella ja 250 opiskelijaa lukiossa. Normaalikoulu toimii kolmessa eri toimipisteessä Oulussa. Harjoittelukoulun tehtävänä on antaa perusopetusta ja lukiokoulutusta, järjestää luokan- ja aineenopettajakoulutuksen pedagogisiin opintoihin kuuluvaa ohjattua opetusharjoittelua, osallistua opettajankoulutuksen kehittämiseen, sekä osallistua oppimista ja opettamista tukevaan tutkimus-, kokeilu- ja kehittämistoimintaan. Järjestämme myös täydennyskoulutusta ja koulutusvientiä. Lisäksi olemme yksi maailman Unesco-kouluista, joiden tavoitteena on muun muassa lisätä kulttuuritietoutta ja edistää suvaitsevaisuutta. Etsimme nyt Oulun normaalikoululle, Linnanmaan yksikköön luokka-asteelle 1-6 Lehtoria, luokanopettajaa määräaikaiseen työsuhteeseen 1.11.2026-31.7.2027 Työtehtävät Etsimme innostunutta opetusalan ammattilaista vahvistamaan työyhteisöämme. Tehtävässä vastaat perusopetuksen opetussuunnitelman mukaisesta opetuksesta luokka-asteella 5 sekä luokanopettajaopiskelijoiden ohjauksesta Oulun yliopiston harjoittelukoulussa. Suunnittelet, toteutat ja arvioit opetusryhmäsi opetusta kokonaisvaltaisesti ja tavoitteellisesti. Oman työsi ja osaamisesi kehittäminen sekä erilaisten sidosryhmien, yhteistyötahojen ja verkostojen kanssa toimiminen kuuluvat tehtäviisi. Mitä tarjoamme? Tuen asiantuntevalta ja innostuneelta tiimiltä, jossa pääset kehittymään ja jakamaan asiantuntemustasi. Liikunta-, kulttuuri- ja hyvinvointietuja (ePassi). Lue lisää muista työsuhde-eduistamme. Ison organisaation tarjoamat kehitys- ja uramahdollisuudet. Merkityksellisen työn ja toimintakulttuurin, jossa sinulla on vapaus työn ja muun elämän yhteensovittamiseen. Lisätietoa työskentelystä Oulun yliopistossa. Tehtävän vaatimukset Tehtävässä edellytetään: harjoittelukoulujen opettajakelpoisuutta (opetustoimen henkilöstön kelpoisuusasetuksen 986/1998 mukainen kelpoisuus sekä tämän lisäksi hyvä opetustaito ja kahden vuoden päätoiminen opettajakokemus opettajaksi valmistumisen jälkeen). Kokemusta opettajan työstä, Vahvaa pedagogista osaamista sekä kykyä kohdata ja ohjata eri kulttuuritaustaisia oppilaita sensitiivisesti Odotamme myös hyviä ryhmänhallintataitoja ja valmiutta työskennellä suurten opetusryhmien kanssa. Sujuvaa suomenkielen kirjallista ja suullista taitoa. Lisäksi eduksi katsotaan: Valmius toteuttaa kielirikasteista opetusta sekä kyvyn hyödyntää monipuolisesti nykyaikaisia opetusmenetelmiä. Opetustehtävien aiempi menestyksekäs hoitaminen Kokemus opetusharjoittelijoiden ohjaamisesta Suuntautuneisuus pedagogiseen tutkimus-, kokeilu- ja kehittämistoimintaan Valmius käyttää tvt-osaamista osana opetusta ja ohjausta sekä toimia mentorina toisille opettajille Kyky opettaa englannin kieltä Arvostamme joustavaa ja kehittämismyönteistä työotetta, kiinnostusta yhteis- ja samanaikaisopettajuuteen sekä hyviä yhteistyö- ja vuorovaikutustaitoja työyhteisössä. Tehtävään valittavan henkilön on esitettävä nähtäväksi rikosrekisterilain 6 §:n 2 momentissa tarkoitettu rikosrekisteriote. Tehtävän palkkaus Tehtävä on määräaikainen 1.11.2026-31.7.2027 ja siihen sovelletaan 4 kuukauden koeaikaa. Tehtävän tehtäväkohtainen palkanosa määräytyy yliopistojen harjoittelukoulujen palkkausjärjestelmän tehtävien vaativuustason 5 perusteella. Lisäksi maksetaan henkilökohtaiseen työstä suoriutumiseen perustuvaa palkanosaa enintään 50 % tehtäväkohtaisesta palkanosasta. Palkka vastaavissa tehtävissä on tyypillisesti 4000-4400 €/kk. Hakeminen Olisiko tässä sinun paikkasi loistaa? Jätä hakemuksesi liitteineen sähköistä hakulomaketta käyttäen viimeistään 30.9.2026. Hakemukseen tulee liittää ansioluettelo (CV) sellaisine liitteineen, joilla hakija haluaa osoittaa kelpoisuutensa ja ansionsa tehtävään sekä hakijan yhteystiedot. Tehtävään parhaiten soveltuvat hakijat kutsutaan haastatteluun. Haastattelut tehtävään järjestetään viikolla 40 ja 41. Tulemme olemaan yhteydessä kaikkiin hakijoihin hakuprosessin aikana. Lisätietoja tehtävästä antaa perusopetuksen apulaisrehtori Janne Pellikainen, 0503271800, janne.pellikainen@oulu.fi Työsuhdemuoto Määräaikainen työsopimus Työsopimus päättyy 2027-07-31 Työsuhteen luonne Kokoaikainen Työsuhteen toivottu aloitusajankohta 1.11.2026 Palkka TES Paikkojen lukumäärä 1 Työllisyysaste 100 Paikkakunta Oulu Maakunta Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Maa Suomi Ilmoitusnumero 2026/553 Yhteys Janne Pellikainen, +358503271800, janne.pellikainen@oulu.fi Julkaistu 16.09.2026 Haku päättyy 30.09.2026 Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Jaa linkki Takaisin avoimiin työpaikkoihin Grade Varbi Recruit rekrytointijärjestelmä Evästeet Ehdot Tietosuojakäytäntö Saavutettavuusseloste × Modal title Käytämme evästeitä sisäänkirjautumiseen, käyttökokemuksen parantamiseen, jakolinkkien tarjoamiseen sekä joissakin tapauksissa markkinointiin ja tilastojen keräämiseen. Hyväksy kaikki evästeet Hyväksy vain tarpeelliset Lue lisää evästeistä tässä ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968536/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Science and Technology Studies (STS) and aquatic restoration in the Nordic and Arctic regions",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Science and Technology Studies (STS) and aquatic restoration in the Nordic and Arctic regions Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher, Science and Technology Studies (STS) and aquatic restoration in the Nordic and Arctic regions Login and apply Faculty of Humanities, History, Culture and Communication Studies The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are looking to hire highly motivated Postdoctoral Researcher to join the Department of Anthropology, in the History, Culture and Communications Unit at the Faculty of Humanities, the University of Oulu. The hired researcher will develop and implement their own research plan in the specified research area and work in collaboration with Dr. Jose A. Cañada and their research team under the programme “Safeguarding biodiversity through interdisciplinary research on habitat restoration” (SAFIRE). Aquatic ecosystems are a central element in how humans are addressing their own survival. Lakes, rivers, wetlands, seas, oceans and melting ice caps are central elements of the ongoing ecological crisis linked to human modes of economic and capitalist production. Discourses and practices of ecological repair coexist with refusals to give up on ideals of economic growth, often featuring techno-optimist visions to develop possible solutions. In this context, restoration of aquatic habitats has emerged with force as a dominant strategy for environmental care, with links to more traditional conservation approaches or more intrusive geoengineering initiatives. The researcher hired will have the opportunity to develop their own research plan to study how the relation between humans and their surrounding environments is shifting as the result of alterations to aquatic ecologies in the Arctic and Nordic regions, with a special focus on knowledge production and practices from technoscientific, regulatory, citizen, and indigenous perspectives. Social research in this area is key to ensure responsible technoscientific development, and socio-ecologically just development of policy and governance. The position benefits from the University of Oulu’s long-term development of trans- and interdisciplinary research about human-environment relations, currently under the programme “Safeguarding biodiversity through interdisciplinary research on habitat restoration” (SAFIRE). As a result, the hired researcher will be an active participant in the exciting calendar of interdisciplinary activities and events. More information about SAFIRE and its research themes can be found here . About the job Hired researcher will work closely with Dr Jose A. Cañada and their research team. The group is conceived as a site for close collaboration among likeminded researchers that also fosters independence and career development. Dynamics of the group build on the CSSM model for distributed and less hierarchical academic collaboration (learn more here ). The team is formed around a common interest in aquatic ecologies and perspectives in the social sciences on care, participation, methodological experimentation, and justice. These areas of interest are articulated around four thematic areas, which all originate in scholarship in the area of Science and Technology Studies: Thematic area 1: A more-than-human approach based on care that serves as a frame diverse practices for environmental management. In this context, management emerges as a form of interaction that requires close contact with other species and habitats. These are practices that are carried out by a variety of actors, including scientific practitioners, environmental managers, governments, civil society organizations, private sector, citizens, and more. Thematic area 2: A broad understanding of knowledge production with an emphasis on flows manifested through practices and discourses that contribute to diverse and situated accounts of the world that do not fit the universalist and positivist approaches that have historically dominated modern science. Knowledge is understood not as fact discovery but as a collective endeavour that takes place across different societal areas and involves human and nonhuman actors. Thematic area 3: Scientific citizenship and public participation in the production of environmental and aquatic futures through hybrid citizen and scientific communities involved in different strategies to know and care for aquatic habitats. This entails understanding the intersectional positioning and situated contributions of different actors, including not just citizen participation in scientific initiatives but the citizen status of experts and interested parties with specific positions towards socioecological debates. Thematic area 4: Methodological experimentation and sensory approaches to develop new lenses and techniques able to yield different results that do not reify normative understandings which, in some cases, can stagnate and polarize environmental debates. This involves relying on modes of knowledge production that step away but continue to engage with scientific methods developed around notions of validity and reliability. The primary duties will include: Planning and conducting social scientiﬁc research on aquatic ecologies that directly engages with at least two of the four thematic areas mentioned above. Participating of and contributing to internal research group activities; planning and implementing collaboration with group colleagues. Producing academic contributions in the form of e.g. articles, monographs, experimental non-textual formats. Active participation and facilitation of interdisciplinary work both in the context of SAFIRE activities and in their own projects. Participating in outreach initiatives that engage both academic and non-academic publics. Engaging in writing and submitting applications for further research funding. Other administrative and community activities linked to academic life at the University of Oulu. What we offer The support of an experienced and enthusiastic team, with whom you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Development and career options of the big organization. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being, and flexible multi-location and remote work opportunities in Finland. Read more about other staff benefits. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. Work that matters! Read more about working with us. Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the position, we require from you: Doctoral degree in a relevant field (science and technology studies, anthropology, sociology, social psychology, environmental social sciences, or equivalent) . The doctoral degree must have been completed by the closing date for applications. The degree must have been obtained no more than 10 years ago. An interest in issues related to environmental management of aquatic habitats in the Nordic and/or Arctic regions Experience in qualitative social scientiﬁc research evidenced by peer-reviewed publications or defended doctoral thesis monograph A transdisciplinary research orientation, with experience of or interest in knowledge communities beyond the social sciences and humanities Capacity to collaborate in research and research dissemination activities Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills in English (the working language of the research team) Proven teamwork skills and commitment to academic collaboration We also appreciate: Conversational level of Finnish When assessing the candidate’s merits for the position of Postdoctoral Researcher, attention will be paid to scientific excellence, such as research outputs, international scientific activities and collaboration, supervision of undergraduate students, pedagogical competence, societal relevance, impact and potential of scientific activities, and services for the academic community. Salary The position is fixed-term for 3 years as of 2nd November 2026 (or as agreed). The salary will be based on the levels 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 3700-4300 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 30th September 2026 (23:59 Finnish local time) through our recruitment system. The application should be written in English and include the following: Letter of motivation (max. 1 page) summarizing your professional experience and expertise and describing why you are interested in the position Research concept paper (max. 2 pages; references do not count towards this limit) for a potential project in the topic of the position. The plan should include a section that discusses its engagement with at least two of the four thematic areas mentioned above Curriculum vitae (max. 4 pages) in accordance with the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of publications , following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland , with up to five key publications relevant to the position marked in bold Contact information of two to three senior/experienced researchers who may be asked to give a personal statement about you The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Dr. Jose A. Cañada (Jose.Canada(at)oulu.fi). Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/570 Published 16.Sep.2026 Last application date 30.Sep.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:969542/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Medical Statistics",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Medical Statistics Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher, Medical Statistics Login and apply Faculty of Medicine, Population Health The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are inviting applications for a Postdoctoral Researcher in Medical Statistics to join us in the Research Unit for Population Health (PoPH), a multidisciplinary research and teaching unit in the Faculty of Medicine. The position is set within Health Dimensions, a multidisciplinary research initiative funded by the Research Council of Finland. Health Dimensions explores the complex, multidimensional nature of human health, with the aim to prevent chronic diseases and multimorbidity through a new level of understanding and acting on these dimensions - lifelong molecular, physiological, environmental, behavioural and societal mechanisms. About the job The successful candidate will join a research group working on longitudinal models of multiple chronic diseases across the life course. The postdoctoral researcher will contribute to building and evaluating machine learning models for multiple chronic diseases in real-world data and cohort studies. To successfully work in this position, experience of data-driven analytical approaches, machine learning and advanced longitudinal modelling utilising real-world health and healthcare data is essential. Key responsibilities Extract, link, clean and manage data from administrative health and healthcare data and other relevant sources Design reproducible studies and evaluate models using appropriate analytical methods Build and evaluate reproducible longitudinal models and research software Write scientific articles and contribute to articles led by other members of a multidisciplinary team Present research findings in scientific meetings at the unit, university and externally Contribute to information governance documentation, project reporting, stakeholder meetings and funding applications Who are you? You will need the following A doctoral degree in health data science, bioinformatics, statistics, computer science or a closely related discipline. Your doctoral degree should be completed by the end of the application period and no longer than 10 years prior. Experience of utilising, evaluating and developing machine learning methods, with strong analytical and programming skills (e.g. R or Python) Experience of undertaking accurate, reproducible data preparation and analysis A track record of peer-reviewed research articles, research software and/or datasets Ability to organise competing priorities and deliver accurate, high-quality work to an agreed timetable Ability to work independently and take responsibility for planning and delivering tasks A collaborative and inclusive approach to interdisciplinary teamwork Excellent written and spoken English We will also appreciate Excellent written and spoken Finnish Familiarity with research computing, virtual server solutions and software development Ability to communicate technical or clinical research concepts clearly to academic and non-academic audiences What we offer The support of a highly experienced and enthusiastic research team and unit, with whom you can share and develop your expertise Career development and learning opportunities in a multidisciplinary, international university setting and within Health Dimensions research initiative Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. Occupational healthcare and social staff benefits. Read more about other staff benefits . University of Oulu has an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu . Contract and salary This is a fixed-term position, with an anticipated starting date of 1 st November 2026 (or as soon as possible thereafter) and an expected end date of 31 st August 2028. The salary will be based on the levels 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff at Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 3900-4200 € per calendar month. A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Please apply by 30 th September 2026 (23:59 Finnish time) using our online recruitment system Varbi. The application should be written in English, and include the following: Cover letter (maximum 1 page), including details of how the post-doctoral position fits in with your experience in data analysis, career development and scientific interests, and a proposed starting date. CV (maximum 2 pages). List of publications (please do not attach copies of manuscripts) Contact details of 2-3 referees , at least one of whom must be your previous line manager / research supervisor Copies of your Master’s degree and PhD certificates . If your degrees are not from an English or Finnish speaking institution, please provide a translation of any documents. Please do not exceed the page limits for the application documents . Interviews (in-person or remotely) will be held in October 2026. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, such as people of different ages, genders, and linguistic, cultural and ethnic groups. University of Oulu is committed to supporting and promoting equality and diversity and to creating an inclusive environment for all. Contact Information For questions, please contact Associate Professor Katriina Heikkila (katriina.heikkila[at]oulu.fi). Please do not send any application documents to this email address. Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/576 Published 18.Sep.2026 Last application date 30.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968632/": {
      "title": "Yliopisto-opettaja, pohjoissaame",
      "description": "Yliopisto-opettaja, pohjoissaame Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Yliopisto-opettaja, pohjoissaame Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Humanistinen tiedekunta, Giellagas-instituutti Oulun yliopisto on monitieteinen, kansainvälisesti toimiva tiedeyliopisto, jonka noin 4000 työntekijää tuottavat korkeatasoiseen tutkimukseen pohjautuvaa uutta tietoa ja antavat tutkimukseen perustuvaa opetusta kestävämmän, älykkäämmän ja inhimillisemmän maailman rakentamiseksi. Oulun yliopistoyhteisössä toimii kaikkiaan noin 19 000 henkilöä. Pohjoisen tiedeyhteisömme toiminta on globaalisti vaikuttavaa ja luo edellytyksiä innovaatioiden syntymiselle. Kaikkea tutkimus-, opetus- ja työyhteisötoimintaamme ohjaavat yliopistomme arvot sekä eettiset periaatteet. Haemme nyt Oulun yliopiston humanistisen tiedekunnan Giellagas-instituuttiin Yliopisto-opettajaa toistaiseksi voimassa olevaan työsuhteeseen 1.1.2027 lähtien. Giellagas-instituutilla on valtakunnallinen vastuu saamen kielten ja saamelaisen kulttuurin ylimmästä opetuksesta ja tutkimuksesta Suomessa. Instituutin saamen kielten oppiaine kouluttaa kielen asiantuntijoita saamelaisyhteisön tarpeisiin. Opinnot tarjoavat mahdollisuuksia kansainväliseen uraan Pohjoismaiden rajat ylittävällä saamelaisalueella. Saamen kielten opinnoissa on kolme linjaa: pohjoissaamen, inarinsaamen ja koltansaamen linja. Pohjoissaamen linja on tarkoitettu äidinkielisille puhujille sekä muille, joilla on hyvä pohjoissaamen taito. Lisäksi instituutissa voi suorittaa 25 opintopisteen laajuiset pohjoissaamen perusopinnot vieraana kielenä. Työtehtävät Yliopisto-opettajana opetat perus-, aine- ja syventäviä opintoja ohjaat ja tarkastat opinnäytetöitä ohjaat opiskelijoita ja neuvot opintoihin liittyvissä asioissa tutkit pohjoissaamen kieltä osallistut hallinnollisten tehtävien hoitoon Mitä tarjoamme? Tuen asiantuntevalta ja innostavalta Giellagas-instituutin työyhteisöltä, jossa pääset kehittymään ja jakamaan asiantuntemustasi. Liikunta-, kulttuuri- ja hyvinvointietuja (ePassi). Lue lisää muista työsuhde-eduistamme . Ison organisaation tarjoamat kehitys- ja uramahdollisuudet. Merkityksellisen työn ja toimintakulttuurin, jossa sinulla on vapaus työn ja muun elämän yhteensovittamiseen. Lisätietoa työskentelystä Oulun yliopistossa . Mitä etsimme? Onnistuaksesi ja viihtyäksesi tehtävässä edellytämme sinulta: Ylempää korkeakoulututkintoa saamen kielten alalta C2-tasoista kirjallista ja suullista pohjoissaamen taitoa Hyvää opetustaitoa Valmiutta tieteelliseen työhön Sujuvaa kirjallista ja suullista suomen kielen taitoa Lisäksi katsomme eduksi: Pedagoginen koulutus Laaja tehtäväalueen osaaminen Muut opetustoimessa saavutetut ansiot Yliopisto-opettajan odotetaan suorittavan kahden vuoden kuluessa työsuhteen alkamisesta vähintään 25 opintopistettä yliopistopedagogisia tai niihin rinnastettavia opintoja, ellei valitulla ole näitä opintoja suoritettuna työsuhteen alkaessa. Palkkaus Tehtävä on toistaiseksi voimassa oleva alkaen 1.1.2027 (tai sopimuksen mukaan). Tehtävä sijoittuu yliopiston palkkausjärjestelmän opetus- ja tutkimushenkilöstön vaativuustasolle 5. Lisäksi maksetaan henkilökohtaiseen suoriutumiseen perustuvaa palkanosaa, joka on enintään 50 % tehtäväkohtaisesta palkanosasta. Palkka vastaavissa tehtävissä on tyypillisesti 3800-4100 EUR/kk. Tehtävässä sovelletaan 6 kuukauden koeaikaa. Kuinka hakea? Jos kiinnostuit, haethan paikkaa rekrytointijärjestelmän kautta viimeistään 18.10.2026 . Liitä hakemukseen mukaan: Hakemuskirje CV Narratiivinen CV käyttäen annettua mallia (lisätietoja Tutkimuksen ja tutkijan arvioinnin periaatteet Oulun yliopistossa ) Julkaisuluettelo Suomen Akatemian pohjan mukaan Opetusportfolio , Oulun yliopiston ohjeiden mukaisesti Tehtävään parhaiten soveltuvat hakijat kutsutaan haastatteluun, joka pidetään etäyhteydellä tai kasvokkain. Opetustaitoa arvioidaan opetusportfolion ja opetusnäytteen perusteella. Opetustaidon arvioinnista on saatava vähintään arvosana ”hyvä” (3/5). Tulemme olemaan yhteydessä kaikkiin hakijoihin hakuprosessin aikana. Lisätietoja Jäikö jokin arveluttamaan? Ota yhteyttä: johtaja Sigga-Marja Magga, humanistinen tiedekunta, Giellagas-instituutti, sigga-marja.magga@oulu.fi, +358 50 568 5326 Sámegillii ohcamuša sáhttá lohkat dáppe. Työsuhdemuoto Toistaiseksi Työsuhteen luonne Kokoaikainen Paikkojen lukumäärä 1 Työllisyysaste 100% Paikkakunta Oulu Maakunta Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Maa Suomi Ilmoitusnumero 2026/573 Julkaistu 21.09.2026 Haku päättyy 18.10.2026 Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Jaa linkki Takaisin avoimiin työpaikkoihin Grade Varbi Recruit rekrytointijärjestelmä Evästeet Ehdot Tietosuojakäytäntö Saavutettavuusseloste × Modal title Käytämme evästeitä sisäänkirjautumiseen, käyttökokemuksen parantamiseen, jakolinkkien tarjoamiseen sekä joissakin tapauksissa markkinointiin ja tilastojen keräämiseen. Hyväksy kaikki evästeet Hyväksy vain tarpeelliset Lue lisää evästeistä tässä ×"
    }
